From 21d1892938398504ca7f3a3f9283af08a48810ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abinash Haldorai <abinash.haldorai@eka.care>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:20:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Voice: let the phone agent hand the call to a person

Add the transfer_to_human tool to the phone pipeline. When a number's
binding has a "handover" config (staff number, optional hours, ring
seconds; written by the console), the agent can pass the call on when the
caller asks for a person, it cannot understand them after two tries, or in
an emergency.

How it moves the call, per Vobiz's Transfer API and Dial docs:
- The tool checks staff hours (declines outside them, telling the agent
  when the team is in) and marks the call; it does not move it.
- HandoverProcessor, between the agent and TTS, waits for the agent's
  reply to end and the caller to have heard it (confirmed by a short
  settle, so a pause between sentences does not count), then POSTs
  {api}/Account/{auth_id}/Call/{call_uuid}/ with legs=aleg and our
  /voice/transfer URL. A timer covers a silent reply; a refusal tells the
  caller and lets the agent offer it again.
- POST /voice/transfer/{session_id} returns a <Dial> to the staff phone,
  caller ID being the Vobiz number the patient dialled.
- POST /voice/transfer-result/{session_id} gets the final Dial status:
  completed hangs up, anything else plays a short apology (English: Vobiz's
  voice list has no Hindi) and hangs up.

Both URLs carry a signed 10-minute token with its own purpose (an
audio-socket token does not open them). The transfer URL returns the staff
number, so the feature is off unless VOICE_TELEPHONY_SECRET, VOBIZ_AUTH_ID,
VOBIZ_AUTH_TOKEN and HOST are set; the reason it is off is logged.

/voice/answer/{uuid} now records which number the call is on. The legacy
?agent_id= answer URL records none, so it offers no handover.

Not tested on a real Vobiz call or with real audio: the Vobiz request and
XML follow its documentation, and the processor is tested with frames fed
by hand.

